{
 "manufacturer": "Sontex",
 "manufacturer_slug": "sontex",
 "model": "Supercal 531 / Superstatic 440 / 449 with Modbus EIA-485 module",
 "model_slug": "supercal-531-modbus-module",
 "short_model": "Supercal 531 Modbus",
 "aliases": [
  "Supercal 531",
  "Superstatic 440",
  "Superstatic 449",
  "Sontex Modbus EIA-485 module",
  "0531P217"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Energy meter (heat / cooling meter)",
 "applies_to": "Sontex Modbus EIA-485 plug-in module in a Supercal 531 integrator or Superstatic 440/449 heat meter, integrator firmware 3.7 or later; user manual V05 (2019-09).",
 "summary": "Sontex's Supercal 531 integrator and the Superstatic 440/449 heat and cooling meters take an optional RS-485 plug-in module that makes them a Modbus RTU or ASCII slave. Settings and the clock are holding registers, meter values are input registers and error flags are discrete inputs. This map covers the settings block, device information, error flags and the IEEE-754 float copies of energy, volume, pulse inputs, power, flow and temperatures, including the Set-Day stored values.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU",
  "ASCII"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baud": 19200,
  "parity": "Even",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "Modicon",
  "note": "The manual says register numbering starts at 1, which is physical address 0 in the telegram, and prints Modicon-style references: 40011 is holding wire address 10, 30103 is input wire address 102, 10001 is discrete input 0. Its own Modbus Poll / ModScan screenshots use the same 30713/30103 references."
 },
 "default_word_order": "CDAB",
 "firmware": "Integrator / meter firmware FW 3.7 or higher",
 "source": {
  "title": "Modbus EIA-485 Module for Supercal 531 and Superstatic 440/449 - Instructions for Use",
  "doc_number": "0531P217 V05",
  "revision_date": "2019-09",
  "url": "https://www.neovac.ch/downloadcenter/document-a9b1ddfb-1182-446f-b1b9-132bdb729345.pdf",
  "unofficial": true,
  "pages": "p. 10 (word swapping example), pp. 12-17 (defaults, changing settings), pp. 30-39 (register tables), pp. 40-45 (read-out examples)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "This is an unaltered Sontex manual hosted by the Swiss distributor NeoVac; Sontex keeps its own copy behind a login-only extranet and does not host it publicly.",
  "Word order: the tables label 32-bit values '(h-l)' but every table footer says Sontex uses l-h ordering, and the word-swapping example (p. 10) puts the low word in the first register (30723) and the high word in the next (30724). The ModScan example also uses 'least significant register first'. All 32-bit values here are therefore CDAB.",
  "Units of the float values follow the unit-code register at the start of each block (e.g. 30101 energy: 18 Wh, 19 kWh, 146 MWh, 126 MJ, 226 GJ, 20 BTU).",
  "Left out: the 'long data point' integer copies (30201-30220, 30401-30420, 30601-30618, 30801-30834). Their value must be divided by 10 to the power of a separate Decimals register (0-3), which cannot be expressed as a fixed scale. The float copies carry the same quantities.",
  "Left out: monthly logs 31001-33266 (32 stored months per quantity, 2 registers each, floats from 31003 and longs from 31203), which are long arrays rather than single points.",
  "40020 Flow control is printed as 'MB_RTU=0, MB_RTU=1' (presumably RTU/ASCII, but the source does not say), so no enum is given. 32-bit integers are given as UINT32 because the source does not mark them signed (it marks signed values explicitly elsewhere).",
  "The same document also covers the BACnet MS/TP module; that part is not used here."
 ],
